      "text": "To determine the values of \\( A \\) and \\( B \\), we need to first understand what each term means in the context of the problem.\n\n### Step 1: Determine \\( A \\)\n\\( A \\) represents the number of four-digit odd numbers. Here are the conditions for a four-digit odd number:\n- It must be a four-digit number.\n- It must be odd, so its last digit must be one of the following: 1, 3, 5, 7, or 9.\n\nThe first five digits can be any digit from 1 to 9 (since a four-digit number cannot start with 0), and the last digit can be one of 5 possible odd digits.\n\nThe number of choices for each digit position:\n- First digit: 9 choices (1-9)\n- Second digit, third digit, fourth digit, fifth digit, sixth digit: 10 choices each (0-9)\n\nThus, the total number of four-digit odd numbers \\( A \\):\n\n\\[ A = 9 \\times 10 \\times 10 \\times 10 = 9000 \\]\n\n### Step 2: Determine \\( B \\)\n\\( B \\) represents the number of four-digit multiples of 5. Here are the conditions for a four-digit multiple of 5:\n- It must be a four-digit number.\n- It must end in 0 or 5.\n\nTo find this, we need to count the number of four-digit multiples of 5 within the range 1000 to 9999.\n\nSince 1000 to 9999 has 9000 numbers, the number of multiples of 5 within this range is:\n\\[ B = \\frac{9000}{5} = 1800 \\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate \\( A + B \\)\nNow we add the values of \\( A \\) and \\( B \\):\n\n\\[ A + B = 9000 + 1800 = 10800 \\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{10800}\n\\]",
